1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:01,719
Millions of people own stocks.

2
00:00:01,769 --> 00:00:03,709
On Robinhood Chain, stocks are tokens,

3
00:00:03,759 --> 00:00:05,646
but a token earns nothing while it sits.

4
00:00:05,696 --> 00:00:07,843
Wall Street holders sell
covered calls for income,

5
00:00:07,893 --> 00:00:09,795
but someone must pick each week's strike,

6
00:00:09,845 --> 00:00:10,835
and you must trust them.

7
00:00:10,885 --> 00:00:11,827
On-chain it's harder:

8
00:00:11,877 --> 00:00:13,595
multipliers easy to apply twice,

9
00:00:13,645 --> 00:00:14,749
weekend price freezes,

10
00:00:14,799 --> 00:00:16,104
pauses, mid-week splits.

11
00:00:16,154 --> 00:00:17,422
So tokens sit idle,

12
00:00:17,472 --> 00:00:19,232
or go to managers nobody can check.

13
00:00:19,282 --> 00:00:21,872
Now imagine an agent picking
the strike each week,

14
00:00:21,922 --> 00:00:23,474
held to the rules by a contract.

15
00:00:23,524 --> 00:00:24,252
This is Strike:

16
00:00:24,303 --> 00:00:25,988
options vaults for stock tokens.

17
00:00:26,038 --> 00:00:27,806
Weekly premium in USDG.

18
00:00:27,856 --> 00:00:30,440
An AI agent picks the
strike, inside a mandate.

19
00:00:30,490 --> 00:00:32,807
Break it, and its bond goes to depositors.

20
00:00:32,857 --> 00:00:34,496
Rust on Stylus does the math.

21
00:00:34,546 --> 00:00:37,301
Live on Robinhood Chain
and Arbitrum Sepolia.

22
00:00:37,351 --> 00:00:38,335
Inside one week:

23
00:00:38,385 --> 00:00:40,501
Depositors fill a vault
with a fixed mandate.

24
00:00:40,551 --> 00:00:43,071
An agent reads it via MCP and dry-runs.

25
00:00:43,121 --> 00:00:45,665
It proposes delta, expiry, size and price.

26
00:00:45,715 --> 00:00:48,364
The Epoch Manager checks it
at guarded oracle prices.

27
00:00:48,414 --> 00:00:50,632
Rust on Stylus solves and
stress-tests the strike.

28
00:00:50,682 --> 00:00:53,371
If it passes, buyers pay premium in USDG.

29
00:00:53,421 --> 00:00:55,577
If not, the bond is slashed to depositors.

30
00:00:55,627 --> 00:00:57,140
Decisions are hashed on-chain;

31
00:00:57,190 --> 00:00:59,892
the agent has an ERC-8004 identity.

32
00:00:59,942 --> 00:01:01,055
Friday's close settles;

33
00:01:01,105 --> 00:01:03,253
depositors get the premium, less a fee.

34
00:01:03,303 --> 00:01:06,413
Same contracts on Robinhood
Chain and Arbitrum Sepolia.

35
00:01:06,463 --> 00:01:08,102
Say Maya opens the Tesla vault.

36
00:01:08,152 --> 00:01:12,161
Its first week sold the $369.86 call:

37
00:01:12,211 --> 00:01:14,171
four options, 10.01 USDG.

38
00:01:14,221 --> 00:01:16,257
At or below the strike, Maya keeps it;

39
00:01:16,307 --> 00:01:19,432
the buyer profits above $372.36.

40
00:01:19,482 --> 00:01:20,881
The limits are in the contract:

41
00:01:20,931 --> 00:01:23,510
Delta 0.10 to 0.35,

42
00:01:23,560 --> 00:01:25,671
at least 95% of fair value,

43
00:01:25,721 --> 00:01:28,057
at least 0.05% yield,

44
00:01:28,107 --> 00:01:29,444
at most 80% sold,

45
00:01:29,494 --> 00:01:30,346
1 to 8 days,

46
00:01:30,396 --> 00:01:31,339
fixed for good.

47
00:01:31,389 --> 00:01:33,199
The playground tests proposals live,

48
00:01:33,249 --> 00:01:33,852
no wallet.

49
00:01:33,902 --> 00:01:36,486
An honest 0.20-delta call: accepted.

50
00:01:36,536 --> 00:01:38,163
A reckless at-the-money strike:

51
00:01:38,213 --> 00:01:39,783
rejected, delta out of band.

52
00:01:39,833 --> 00:01:43,719
A real one costs the agent
10 USDG, paid to depositors.

53
00:01:43,769 --> 00:01:45,799
Run the agent does the rule
stages live, in your browser,

54
00:01:45,849 --> 00:01:48,718
against the real vault, sending nothing.

55
00:01:49,369 --> 00:01:51,047
Buyers pay at the moment they buy:

56
00:01:51,097 --> 00:01:53,693
oracle spot moved 0.5% against them,

57
00:01:53,743 --> 00:01:55,880
Black-Scholes, times the agent's factor.

58
00:01:55,930 --> 00:01:57,347
Never below intrinsic value,

59
00:01:57,397 --> 00:01:59,355
so stale prices can't be picked off.

60
00:01:59,405 --> 00:02:00,990
Buying waits for the NYSE open,

61
00:02:01,040 --> 00:02:02,701
shown in your own time zone.

62
00:02:02,751 --> 00:02:06,467
Live on September 29, the seller
agent asked for 0.20 delta;

63
00:02:06,517 --> 00:02:10,249
the contract solved $369.86, accepted.

64
00:02:10,299 --> 00:02:12,471
A reckless agent forced
an at-the-money put:

65
00:02:12,521 --> 00:02:14,430
rejected, 10 USDG slashed,

66
00:02:14,480 --> 00:02:15,987
bond 60 to 50.

67
00:02:16,037 --> 00:02:19,176
The explorer says Success:
a rejection isn't a revert,

68
00:02:19,226 --> 00:02:21,200
and 10 USDG left the bond.

69
00:02:21,250 --> 00:02:23,722
The call expired Friday at 20:00 UTC;

70
00:02:23,772 --> 00:02:24,804
it has not settled yet.

71
00:02:24,854 --> 00:02:27,662
It settles at the first mainnet
Chainlink print after expiry;

72
00:02:27,712 --> 00:02:29,644
the contract rejects any other price.

73
00:02:29,694 --> 00:02:32,804
The last print, at 19:55,
came before expiry.

74
00:02:32,854 --> 00:02:35,124
The epoch trace shows
each step's transaction,

75
00:02:35,174 --> 00:02:36,288
and what is pending.

76
00:02:36,338 --> 00:02:38,543
Anyone can run an agent,
with no permission.

77
00:02:38,593 --> 00:02:40,503
Here a test wallet registers an agent

78
00:02:40,553 --> 00:02:43,182
and bonds 60 USDG, above the 50 minimum.

79
00:02:43,232 --> 00:02:44,451
The wallet signs each step:

80
00:02:44,501 --> 00:02:45,784
register, then bond.

81
00:02:45,834 --> 00:02:48,957
Each one waits for its block
on Robinhood Chain testnet.

82
00:02:49,157 --> 00:02:50,259
Now it can propose.

83
00:02:50,309 --> 00:02:53,517
Every rejected proposal costs it 10 USDG.

84
00:02:57,238 --> 00:02:59,268
On Arbitrum Sepolia, Claude planned it:

85
00:02:59,318 --> 00:03:01,873
via Strike's MCP server, it read the vault

86
00:03:01,923 --> 00:03:03,572
and dry-ran five candidates.

87
00:03:03,622 --> 00:03:07,087
It chose 0.20 delta at 105% of fair value,

88
00:03:07,137 --> 00:03:08,073
and wrote why:

89
00:03:08,123 --> 00:03:09,956
mid-band, safe from small moves.

90
00:03:10,006 --> 00:03:13,472
The contract solved $364.29: accepted.

91
00:03:13,522 --> 00:03:14,213
On Arbiscan:

92
00:03:14,263 --> 00:03:16,139
a successful call from the agent's signer.

93
00:03:16,189 --> 00:03:18,662
The same run slashed a
reckless put 10 USDG,

94
00:03:18,712 --> 00:03:20,350
and a buyer took all 4 calls.

95
00:03:20,400 --> 00:03:21,158
In 3D:

96
00:03:21,208 --> 00:03:24,049
Across, Tesla's price. Back, days left.

97
00:03:24,099 --> 00:03:25,449
Up, a share's value.

98
00:03:25,499 --> 00:03:29,193
At expiry it bends flat
at the $364.29 strike:

99
00:03:29,243 --> 00:03:30,597
upside goes to the buyer.

100
00:03:30,647 --> 00:03:34,379
Below, the depositor keeps
stock plus $2.23 per option.

101
00:03:34,429 --> 00:03:36,496
The math is Rust, on Arbitrum Stylus.

102
00:03:36,546 --> 00:03:38,890
Solving a strike takes
48 Black-Scholes runs:

103
00:03:38,941 --> 00:03:41,152
6.5 times less gas than Solidity,

104
00:03:41,202 --> 00:03:43,381
3.3 times less per proposal.

105
00:03:43,431 --> 00:03:45,006
Every run leaves a decision record.

106
00:03:45,056 --> 00:03:47,011
Its hash is anchored in the DecisionLog;

107
00:03:47,062 --> 00:03:49,160
rehash the file, and it matches the chain.

108
00:03:49,210 --> 00:03:51,122
CI re-checks every cited transaction:

109
00:03:51,172 --> 00:03:54,623
177 of 177 verified.

110
00:03:54,673 --> 00:03:56,324
The agent now runs five stages:

111
00:03:56,374 --> 00:03:59,447
market, risk, strike planner,
critic, then the contract.

112
00:03:59,497 --> 00:04:02,844
In this Claude-planned dry run,
four passed and nothing was sent;

113
00:04:02,895 --> 00:04:04,563
its token use is on record.

114
00:04:04,613 --> 00:04:06,958
On the weekend, the market
analyst said no trade;

115
00:04:07,008 --> 00:04:08,329
the rest never ran.

116
00:04:08,379 --> 00:04:09,801
Agent two's accepted put:

117
00:04:09,851 --> 00:04:11,804
each mandate rule, with the headroom left.

118
00:04:11,854 --> 00:04:12,908
Why not the other strikes:

119
00:04:12,958 --> 00:04:15,465
the same proposal at each
delta, judged by the rules.

120
00:04:15,515 --> 00:04:16,649
What would make the week lose:

121
00:04:16,699 --> 00:04:20,132
TSLA below $340.20, 17% model odds,

122
00:04:20,182 --> 00:04:22,043
then stress rows and what-ifs.

123
00:04:22,093 --> 00:04:23,888
Agent one's forced put was rejected:

124
00:04:23,939 --> 00:04:26,715
the check stops at the delta
band; later rules never run.

125
00:04:26,765 --> 00:04:28,701
Its ERC-8004 identity:

126
00:04:28,751 --> 00:04:33,358
114 on Robinhood Chain testnet,
253 on Arbitrum Sepolia.

127
00:04:33,408 --> 00:04:33,977
The monitor,

128
00:04:34,027 --> 00:04:35,047
live on mainnet:

129
00:04:35,097 --> 00:04:39,461
Nvidia's multiplier, 1.000775,
is already in the price,

130
00:04:39,511 --> 00:04:41,359
so Strike never applies it twice.

131
00:04:41,409 --> 00:04:43,857
Over 403 weeks since 2019,

132
00:04:43,907 --> 00:04:46,926
covered calls cut volatility 25 to 46%,

133
00:04:46,976 --> 00:04:48,456
but lagged holding everywhere:

134
00:04:48,506 --> 00:04:52,502
Tesla 23.1% a year, against 44.0% held.

135
00:04:52,552 --> 00:04:54,377
And it assumes full weekly sales.

136
00:04:54,427 --> 00:04:55,241
The proof page:

137
00:04:55,291 --> 00:04:57,609
1,574 tests and proofs,

138
00:04:57,659 --> 00:04:59,465
99.3% line coverage,

139
00:04:59,515 --> 00:05:00,644
nine Halmos proofs,

140
00:05:00,694 --> 00:05:02,522
all 11 review findings fixed.

141
00:05:02,572 --> 00:05:04,408
Running by itself reads both testnets:

142
00:05:04,458 --> 00:05:05,713
prices, each vault's week,

143
00:05:05,763 --> 00:05:06,780
the scheduled jobs.

144
00:05:06,830 --> 00:05:09,052
The mirror audit checks
every copied price:

145
00:05:09,102 --> 00:05:11,904
84 of 84 rounds match mainnet Chainlink.

146
00:05:11,954 --> 00:05:13,683
9 lessons from the live runs,

147
00:05:13,733 --> 00:05:16,177
each with evidence, the fix and its test.

148
00:05:16,227 --> 00:05:17,179
Who else is here?

149
00:05:17,229 --> 00:05:20,278
Stonkhouse and Archer Markets on
Robinhood Chain are order books:

150
00:05:20,328 --> 00:05:21,922
traders pick strike and price.

151
00:05:21,972 --> 00:05:25,069
Ribbon, Derive and Thetanuts
sell crypto options

152
00:05:25,119 --> 00:05:26,722
by auction, order book or RFQ.

153
00:05:26,772 --> 00:05:29,223
Tilt's AI manages vaults, with no options;

154
00:05:29,273 --> 00:05:32,242
its sources don't say
what limits it on-chain.

155
00:05:32,292 --> 00:05:34,300
In Strike, a bonded agent proposes,

156
00:05:34,350 --> 00:05:36,166
the contract enforces mandate and price,

157
00:05:36,216 --> 00:05:37,438
and rule-breakers pay.

158
00:05:37,488 --> 00:05:39,571
Stock-token traps are handled on-chain.

159
00:05:39,621 --> 00:05:41,616
Holders get income and keep their keys.

160
00:05:41,666 --> 00:05:44,638
Weekend freezes: settle on
the first post-expiry price.

161
00:05:44,688 --> 00:05:46,981
Multiplier: never applied, fork-tested.

162
00:05:47,031 --> 00:05:49,704
Agent trust: fixed
mandate, bond, slashing.

163
00:05:49,754 --> 00:05:52,540
Gas: Rust on Stylus, 6.5 times cheaper.

164
00:05:52,590 --> 00:05:54,933
Not done: no audit, and testnet only.

165
00:05:54,983 --> 00:05:57,306
Next: eight settled
weeks, an external audit,

166
00:05:57,356 --> 00:05:59,136
then one capped mainnet vault.

167
00:05:59,186 --> 00:06:01,600
Strike: options on Robinhood
Chain and Arbitrum,

168
00:06:01,650 --> 00:06:03,772
run by agents held to a mandate.
